# Pocket Inventory HUD — Walkthrough

## Summary

Replaced the existing flat-colored `WorldHUD` with a new pixel-art HUD built from the **POCKET INVENTORY (MAIN)** sprite pack. The new HUD is a tabbed device interface with 5 pages, animated light flicker, and page-flip transitions.

## Changes Made

### 1. [HUDAssetLibrary.gd](file:///c:/Users/Zerato/OneDrive/Documents/arccross_system/UI/HUD/HUDAssetLibrary.gd)

**Added 18 new path constants** for all sprite categories:
- `SIDE_TABS_ROOT`, `BUTTONS_ROOT`, `UI_BUTTONS_ROOT`, `HOLDERS_ROOT`, `PROGRESS_BARS_ROOT`
- `CLOCK_ROOT`, `COMPASS_ROOT`, `BULB_ROOT`, `POWER_HUB_ROOT`, `PIXEL_MAP_BASE_ROOT`
- `LIGHT_FLICKER_ROOT`, `PAGE_FLIP_NEXT_ROOT`, `PAGE_FLIP_PREV_ROOT`, `PIXEL_MAP_FRAME`

**Added 13 new static accessor methods**:
- `side_tab_texture(index)`, `button_sprite(index)`, `ui_button_sprite(index)`
- `holder_texture(index)`, `progress_bar_texture(index)`
- `clock_texture(index)`, `compass_texture(index)`, `bulb_texture(index)`, `power_hub_texture(index)`
- `pixel_map_base_texture(index)`, `pixel_map_frame_texture()`
- `light_flicker_frames()` — batch loads 16 animation frames
- `page_flip_frames(direction)` — batch loads 11 transition frames

All existing methods and constants are **untouched** so nothing breaks in `InventoryUI`, `MedicalMonitor`, or the combat UI.

