### 2. [WorldHUD.gd](file:///c:/Users/Zerato/OneDrive/Documents/arccross_system/UI/HUD/WorldHUD.gd) — Full Rewrite

The script was completely rewritten while **preserving the exact public API**:

| API Element | Status |
|---|---|
| `class_name WorldHUD` | ✅ Preserved |
| `signal inventory_requested` | ✅ Preserved |
| `signal save_requested` | ✅ Preserved |
| `signal load_requested` | ✅ Preserved |
| `func show_snapshot(snapshot)` | ✅ Preserved |
| `func set_inventory_open(open)` | ✅ Preserved |

**New internal architecture:**

- **Device Frame** — `TextureRect` using `Pixel Map/0.png` (the full pixel-art device), scaled by `PIX = 3.0`
- **Light Flicker Overlay** — `TextureRect` cycling through 16 frames at 0.15s intervals, rendered at 12% opacity
- **5 Side Tab Buttons** — `TextureButton` strip using `Side Tabs/` sprites, swapping normal/active textures
- **5 Page Views** (toggle visibility on tab click):
  - **Profile** — Title, vital bars (blood/stance/hunger/thirst/fatigue/temperature), warning label, INV/MED quick buttons
  - **Inventory** — Simple page that emits `inventory_requested` to open the full `InventoryUI`
  - **World Map** — Title + grid background display
  - **Save/Load** — Save/Load buttons that emit the respective signals
  - **Options** — Scanline toggle, HUD scale slider
- **Clock Widget** — `TextureRect` with time label overlay in the left gadget strip
- **Compass Widget** — `TextureRect` with location label overlay
- **Bottom Bar** — 3 decorative `TextureButton`s
- **MedicalMonitor** — Instantiated from scene programmatically, preserving M-key toggle

**Page transitions** use `page_flip_frames()` for a smooth animated page turn.

